sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-029: Reauthentication for Sensitive Changes — Sequence Diagram
    actor OWNER as PART or ADMIN Owner
    participant UI as React Card + ReauthenticationPanel
    participant FB as Firebase Auth
    participant API as Express Auth API + Guards
    participant OTP as Email OTP Service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL / Supabase

    OWNER->>UI: Start sensitive action (setup, restart, replace, regenerate, or disable)
    UI->>API: Original protected request
    API->>API: Recent-auth check on Firebase auth_time (≤ 600 s)
    API-->>UI: 401 REAUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED, nothing changed
    UI->>UI: Keep intended action in memory and show Verify identity

    alt Owner cancels
        UI-->>OWNER: Verification cancelled, no changes made
    else Step 1 — primary sign-in
        OWNER->>UI: Enter current password or choose linked provider
        UI->>FB: Reauthenticate the signed-in user
        alt Wrong password, mismatched account, or popup closed
            FB-->>UI: Firebase error
            UI-->>OWNER: Safe message, password field cleared
        else Primary sign-in confirmed
            FB-->>UI: New ID token with a new auth_time
            Note over UI,API: mfa_auth_time no longer matches, so protected routes return MFA_REQUIRED
            UI->>API: POST /api/auth/mfa/challenge
            API->>OTP: Issue code (lock and fresh-auth checks)
            OTP->>DB: Store hashed 10-minute challenge
            OTP-->>OWNER: Email 6-digit code
            OWNER->>UI: Enter email code (Step 2)
            UI->>API: POST /api/auth/mfa/verify
            API->>DB: Reserve serialized attempt before comparing
            alt Already locked or five earlier failures
                DB-->>API: Reject without comparing the OTP
                API-->>UI: 423 ACCOUNT_LOCKED with retry time
                UI-->>OWNER: 15-minute lock, action never retried
            else Comparison slot reserved (attempts 1–5)
                API->>API: Compare code with the stored challenge hash
                alt Code incorrect
                    API->>DB: Keep reserved attempt as failed
                    alt Fifth failed attempt
                        API->>DB: Invalidate pending challenges
                        API-->>UI: 423 ACCOUNT_LOCKED with retry time
                    else Attempts 1–4
                        API-->>UI: Safe invalid-code response
                    end
                else Code accepted
                    API->>DB: Consume challenge and mark attempt successful
                    API->>FB: Set mfa_auth_time = new auth_time
                    API-->>UI: Verified
                    UI->>FB: Force-refresh ID token
                    UI->>API: Retry the original request once
                    API->>API: Server re-checks recent auth and MFA
                    API-->>UI: Action result
                    UI-->>OWNER: Return to the authenticator flow
                end
            end
        end
    end

    Note over UI,DB: Locked attempts are rejected before comparison. After 15 minutes, an auth_time older than the lock end returns FRESH_AUTH_REQUIRED.
